# Mod versioning

Each mod has its own `About.xml` `modVersion` (`MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`). Bump **only the mod you changed**. Read the current number from `About.xml` and add the bump — do not invent a line (Deep Colony is **1.5.x**). Player.log reads this number.

## When to bump

| Change | Bump |
|---|---|
| Breaking / big content era | `+1.0.0` (major) |
| New player-facing feature | `+0.1.0` (minor). Reset patch to 0. |
| Bugfix / compat glue / copy | `+0.0.1` (patch) |

Examples: Empty Nest firing on newborns was **1.5.1**. Last-of-the-line death gate → **1.5.2**. A new family system → **1.6.0**. A full rewrite → **2.0.0** only if asked.

## Also update

- That mod's `About/changelog.txt` (Steam paste = this version only). First line of the current block **must start with this `modVersion`** so Add Changenote can replace Steam's auto text — see `add-changenote-changelog.mdc`.
- That mod's `CHANGELOG.md` player-facing version line
- Do **not** bump unrelated mods. Do not skip the bump because a build stamp exists.
